{
  "title": "Namaz of Imam Zayn al-Abidin (a.s.)",
  "data": "Upon concluding the prayer, say the following supplication:\nيَا مَنْ اَظْهَرَ الْجَميلَ\nYAA MAN AZHARAL JAMEEL\nO He Who has shown only goodness\nوَسَتَرَ الْقَبيحَ\nWA SATARAL QABEEH\nand concealed the evil (deeds of His servants)!\nيَا مَنْ لَمْ يُؤَاخِذْ بِالْجَرِيرَةِ\nYAA MAN LAM YU'AAKHIDH BIL JAREERAH\nO He Who has not censured for the offenses\nوَلَمْ يَهْتِكِ السِّتْرَ\nWA LAM YAHTIKIS SITR\nand has not exposed the hidden!\nيَا عَظِيمَ الْعَفْوِ\nYAA A'ZEEMAL A'FW\nO He Who is Ample in pardoning!\nيَا حَسَنَ التَّجَاوُزِ\nYAA HASANAT TAJAAWUZ\nO He Who is Excellent in overlooking!\nيَا وَاسِعَ الْمَغْفِرَةِ\nYAA WAASI'AL MAGHFIRAH\nO He Who is Liberal in forgiving!\nيَا بَاسِطَ الْيَدَيْنِ بِالرَّحْمَةِ\nYAA BAASITAL YADAYNI BIR RAHMAH\nO He Who opens His hands wide with mercy!\nيَا صَاحِبَ كُلِّ نَجْوَىٰ\nYAA SAAHIBA KULLI NAJWAA\nO He Who is present in all confidential talks!\nيَا مُنْتَهَىٰ كُلِّ شَكْوَىٰ\nYAA MUNTAHAA KULLI SHAKWAA\nO He Who is the ultimate objective of all complaints!\nيَا كَرِيـمَ الصَّفْحِ\nYAA KAREEMAS SAFH\nO He Who is Generous in condonation!\nيَا عَظِيمَ الرَّجَاءِ\nYAA A'ZEEMAR RAJAA'\nO He Who is greatly hoped!\nيَا مُبْتَدِئاً بِالنِّعَمِ قَبْلَ اسْتِحْقَاقِهَا\nYAA MUBTADI'AN BIN NI'AMI QABLAS TIHQAAQIHAA\nO He Who takes the initiative in favoring before they are deserved!\nيَا رَبَّنَا وَسَيِّدَنَا وَمَوْلَانَا\nYAA RABBANAA WA SAYYIDANAA WA MAWLAANAA\nO our Lord, our Master, and our Chief!\nيَا غَايَةَ رَغْبَتِنَا\nYAA GHAAYATA RAGHBATINAA\nO He Who is the ultimate of our desires!\nاَسْاَلُكَ اللَّهُمَّ اَنْ تُصَلِّيَ عَلَىٰ مُحَمَّدٍ وَآلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nAS'ALUKAL LAAHUMMA AN TUSALLIYA A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\nI beseech You, O Allah, to send blessings to Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad.",
  "merits": "In his book of Jamal al-Usbu', Sayyid Ibn Tawus has recorded a special prayer and supplication for each of the Holy Imams (a.s.), to be offered on Fridays.\nImam Zayn al-Abidin (a.s.)'s prayer consists of four units. In each unit, recite [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) once and [Surah al-Tawhid](A116) one hundred times."
}
